 "interpretation": {
  "text": "Assuming one effect shared by all 13 studies, the odds of tuberculosis in the vaccinated groups were 0.62 times the odds in the unvaccinated groups (95% CI 0.57 to 0.68). Odds are not risks, so this is not a risk ratio; the two differ most when the event is common.",
